Dear Sedona--

I have attached an official letter conditionally accepting you into the
SEAS-CC 4-1 Program. The letter outlines what you have left to do in the
Core Curriculum (just the swim test, if it is not waived this year) and
directs you to meet with your departmental and CSA advisors to ensure that
you are on track to earn your SEAS BS in May 2022. (The offer is
"conditional" in the sense that it would be withdrawn if you did not
complete your SEAS BS and all parts of the Core on schedule.)

Congratulations, and please let me know if you have any questions.

Best,

Nancy Workman, PhD

Advising Dean

Columbia College/Columbia Engineering

James H. and Christine Turk Berick Center for Student Advising

403 Lerner Hall

Columbia University

New York, NY 10027

 Direct line: 212-851-9122

Fax: 212-854-2458

 *To schedule an advising appointment:
**http://studentaffairs.columbia.edu/csa/appointments
<http://studentaffairs.columbia.edu/csa/appointments>*

*FAQs on Fall 2020: https://www.college.columbia.edu/fall-2020-faqs
<https://www.college.columbia.edu/fall-2020-faqs>*

